{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/4575289.Leigh_Bardugo", "name": "Leigh Bardugo", "birthDate": "0001-04-06 00:00:00", "genres": ["Young Adult", "Science Fiction & Fantasy", "Historical Fiction"], "avgRating": 4.16, "reviewsCount": 538165, "ratingsCount": 4896757, "about": "Leigh Bardugo is the #1 New York Times bestselling author of Ninth House and the creator of the Grishaverse (now a Netflix original series) which spans the Shadow and Bone trilogy, the Six of Crows duology, the King of Scars duology\u2014and much more. Her short fiction has appeared in multiple anthologies including The Best American Science Fiction and Fantasy. She lives in Los Angeles and is an associate fellow of Pauli Murray College at Yale University. For information on new releases and appearances, sign up for her newsletter.She would be delighted if you visited her at LeighBardugo.com and fairly giddy if you liked her selfies on Instagram. Leigh Bardugo is the #1 New York Times bestselling author of Ninth House and the creator of the Grishaverse (now a Netflix original series) which spans the Shadow and Bone trilogy, the Six of Crows duology, the King of Scars duology\u2014and much more. Her short fiction has appeared in multiple anthologies including The Best American Science Fiction and Fantasy. She lives in Los Angeles and is an associate fellow of Pauli Murray College at Yale University. For information on new releases and appearances, sign up for her newsletter.She would be delighted if you visited her at LeighBardugo.com and fairly giddy if you liked her selfies on Instagram. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/1834559.Karl_Braungart", "name": "Karl Braungart", "genres": ["Mystery", "Fiction", "Contemporary"], "avgRating": 4.3, "reviewsCount": 55, "ratingsCount": 13844, "about": "Born in Baltimore, Maryland, Karl grew up in the Catonsville area with four siblings. While in the US Army and living in Germany, Karl gained hands-on experience in military intelligence during the Cold War. He worked in the administration of a security intelligence department, assisting soldiers completing security clearances and fingerprinting before submitting to the FBI for verification. The military work also entailed seminar training to familiarize MI soldiers about Soviet/Russian espionage. Because the MI work also included driving the CO to intelligence meetings in Stuttgart, he was able to attend some meetings related to espionage matters as a bystander. While stationed overseas, Karl's travels throughout Europe helped develop his Born in Baltimore, Maryland, Karl grew up in the Catonsville area with four siblings. While in the US Army and living in Germany, Karl gained hands-on experience in military intelligence during the Cold War. He worked in the administration of a security intelligence department, assisting soldiers completing security clearances and fingerprinting before submitting to the FBI for verification. The military work also entailed seminar training to familiarize MI soldiers about Soviet/Russian espionage. Because the MI work also included driving the CO to intelligence meetings in Stuttgart, he was able to attend some meetings related to espionage matters as a bystander. While stationed overseas, Karl's travels throughout Europe helped develop his understanding of foreign cultural differences. After serving, Karl worked full-time and part-time in commercial construction for financial support during college. He spent .seven years working in this area; attaining journeyman status. He graduated from the University of Maryland, College Park, majoring in Political Science (International Affairs, Comparative Government), and minored in English Literature. After college, Karl worked as a construction manager for construction and engineering firms. Karl has spent the last several decades maintaining his awareness of Middle East politics and social movements. Before retiring, Karl began to fulfill a long-held desire to write novels. Now fully retired, he has written four, one family saga and three espionage novels. He is in progress of writing the fourth spy novel. Karl is a member of the Eastern Shore Writers Association, the Rehoboth Beach Writers Guild, and the Maryland Writers Association. He attends the Creatures, Crime and Creativity conference annually as well as many others. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/137261.Barbara_W_Tuchman", "name": "Barbara W. Tuchman", "birthDate": "1912-01-30 00:00:00", "deathDate": "1989-02-06 00:00:00", "genres": ["Biography", "History"], "avgRating": 4.12, "reviewsCount": 7738, "ratingsCount": 147908, "about": "Barbara Wertheim Tuchman, historian, won a Pulitzer Prize for The Guns of August (1962) and for Stilwell and the American Experience in China (1971). This author and double self-trained. People best know the prelude and first month of World War I. As an author, Tuchman focused on popular production. Her clear, dramatic storytelling covered topics as diverse as the 14th century and World War I and sold millions of copies. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbara... Barbara Wertheim Tuchman, historian, won a Pulitzer Prize for The Guns of August (1962) and for Stilwell and the American Experience in China (1971). This author and double self-trained. People best know the prelude and first month of World War I. As an author, Tuchman focused on popular production. Her clear, dramatic storytelling covered topics as diverse as the 14th century and World War I and sold millions of copies. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbara... ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/13477444.Vince_Milam", "name": "Vince Milam", "genres": ["Mystery", "Suspense", "Thriller"], "avgRating": 4.46, "reviewsCount": 1093, "ratingsCount": 30089, "about": "To tell a good tale. It\u2019s a simple and valid answer when the question pops up, \u201cWhy do you write?\u201dAt the end of the day, it is to tell a good tale.Vince Milam has lived all over the world, traipsing through the Amazon, Congo, and Papua New Guinea\u2014all the while demonstrating bourbon has medicinal qualities. Raised in Texas, he lives in the mountainous West where he proves\u2014annually\u2014that God doesn\u2019t want us driving on snow. He relishes great reads, fine trout streams, family, old friends, and\u2014especially\u2014writing fast-paced thrillers that keep you up at night."}
