{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/4043.Wilbur_Smith", "name": "Wilbur Smith", "birthDate": "1933-01-09 00:00:00", "deathDate": "2021-11-13 00:00:00", "genres": ["Literature & Fiction", "Historical Fiction", "Mystery & Thrillers"], "avgRating": 4.11, "reviewsCount": 14157, "ratingsCount": 357279, "about": "Wilbur Smith was the bestselling author of many novels, each researched on his numerous expeditions worldwide. His bestselling Courtney series includes Assegai, The Sound of Thunder, Birds of Prey, Monsoon, and Blue Horizon. His other books include Those in Peril, River God, Warlock, The Seventh Scroll, and The Sunbird. His books have been translated into twenty-six languages and have sold over 120 million copies. Smith was born to a British family in Northern Rhodesia, now Zambia, in Central Africa, and attended Rhodes University in South Africa. By the time of his death in 2021 he had published 49 books and had sold more than 140 million copies. Wilbur Smith died at his Cape Town home on November 13, 2021. He was 88 years old at the time Wilbur Smith was the bestselling author of many novels, each researched on his numerous expeditions worldwide. His bestselling Courtney series includes Assegai, The Sound of Thunder, Birds of Prey, Monsoon, and Blue Horizon. His other books include Those in Peril, River God, Warlock, The Seventh Scroll, and The Sunbird. His books have been translated into twenty-six languages and have sold over 120 million copies. Smith was born to a British family in Northern Rhodesia, now Zambia, in Central Africa, and attended Rhodes University in South Africa. By the time of his death in 2021 he had published 49 books and had sold more than 140 million copies. Wilbur Smith died at his Cape Town home on November 13, 2021. He was 88 years old at the time of his death. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/600.Robert_T_Kiyosaki", "name": "Robert T. Kiyosaki", "birthDate": "1947-04-08 00:00:00", "genres": ["Business & Investing"], "avgRating": 4.1, "reviewsCount": 31792, "ratingsCount": 801344, "about": "Robert Toru Kiyosaki is an American businessman and author, known for the Rich Dad Poor Dad series of personal finance books. He is the founder of the Rich Dad Company, a private financial education company that provides personal finance and business education to people through books and videos, and Rich Global LLC, which filed for bankruptcy in 2012.Since 2010, Kiyosaki was the subject of a class action suit filed by people who attended his seminars, and the subject of investigative documentaries by the CBC, WTAE-TV and CBS News. In January 2024, Kiyosaki revealed that he was more than $1 billion dollars in debt."}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/22796.Laurence_Sterne", "name": "Laurence Sterne", "birthDate": "1713-11-24 00:00:00", "deathDate": "1768-03-18 00:00:00", "genres": ["Fiction"], "influences": ["Monta", "Alexander Pope", "Cervantes", "Rabelais", "John Locke", "Jonathan Swift", "Montaigne"], "avgRating": 3.64, "reviewsCount": 2154, "ratingsCount": 29637, "about": "Laurence Sterne was an Irish-born English novelist and an Anglican clergyman. He is best known for his novels The Life and Opinions of Tristram Shandy, Gentleman, and A Sentimental Journey Through France and Italy; but he also published many sermons, wrote memoirs, and was involved in local politics. Sterne died in London after years of fighting consumption (tuberculosis).See also http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurence... Laurence Sterne was an Irish-born English novelist and an Anglican clergyman. He is best known for his novels The Life and Opinions of Tristram Shandy, Gentleman, and A Sentimental Journey Through France and Italy; but he also published many sermons, wrote memoirs, and was involved in local politics. Sterne died in London after years of fighting consumption (tuberculosis).See also http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurence... ...more"}
