{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/24556.Sara_Gruen", "name": "Sara Gruen", "genres": ["Literary Fiction", "Contemporary", "Historical Fiction"], "avgRating": 4.07, "reviewsCount": 77955, "ratingsCount": 1755104, "about": "Sara Gruen is the #1 New York Times and USA Today bestselling author of five novels: AT THE WATER'S EDGE, APE HOUSE, WATER FOR ELEPHANTS, RIDING LESSONS, and FLYING CHANGES. Her works have been translated into forty-three languages, and have sold more than ten million copies worldwide. WATER FOR ELEPHANTS was adapted into a major motion picture in 2011 starring Reese Witherspoon, Rob Pattinson, and Christoph Waltz, and then into a smash Broadway musical, currently running at the Imperial Theatre, written by Rick Elice and PigPen Theatre Co. and directed by Jessica Stone.She lives in Western North Carolina with her husband and three sons, along with their dogs, cats, horses, birds, and the world\u2019s fussiest goat. Sara Gruen is the #1 New York Times and USA Today bestselling author of five novels: AT THE WATER'S EDGE, APE HOUSE, WATER FOR ELEPHANTS, RIDING LESSONS, and FLYING CHANGES. Her works have been translated into forty-three languages, and have sold more than ten million copies worldwide. WATER FOR ELEPHANTS was adapted into a major motion picture in 2011 starring Reese Witherspoon, Rob Pattinson, and Christoph Waltz, and then into a smash Broadway musical, currently running at the Imperial Theatre, written by Rick Elice and PigPen Theatre Co. and directed by Jessica Stone.She lives in Western North Carolina with her husband and three sons, along with their dogs, cats, horses, birds, and the world\u2019s fussiest goat. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/4379.Sylvia_Plath", "name": "Sylvia Plath", "birthDate": "1932-10-27 00:00:00", "deathDate": "1963-02-11 00:00:00", "genres": ["Poetry", "Literature & Fiction", "Biographies & Memoirs"], "influences": ["Anne Sexton", "Emily Dickinson", "Emily Bront\u00eb", "William Blake", "W.H. Auden", "W.B. Yeats", "Virginia Woolf", "Theodore Roethke", "Robert Lowell", "Dylan Thomas"], "avgRating": 4.08, "reviewsCount": 72484, "ratingsCount": 1205622, "about": "Sylvia Plath was an American poet, novelist, and short story writer. Known primarily for her poetry, Plath also wrote a semi-autobiographical novel, The Bell Jar, under the pseudonym Victoria Lucas. The book's protagonist, Esther Greenwood, is a bright, ambitious student at Smith College who begins to experience a mental breakdown while interning for a fashion magazine in New York. The plot parallels Plath's experience interning at Mademoiselle magazine and subsequent mental breakdown and suicide attempt. Sylvia Plath was an American poet, novelist, and short story writer. Known primarily for her poetry, Plath also wrote a semi-autobiographical novel, The Bell Jar, under the pseudonym Victoria Lucas. The book's protagonist, Esther Greenwood, is a bright, ambitious student at Smith College who begins to experience a mental breakdown while interning for a fashion magazine in New York. The plot parallels Plath's experience interning at Mademoiselle magazine and subsequent mental breakdown and suicide attempt. ...more"}
