{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/32878.Michel_Houellebecq", "name": "Michel Houellebecq", "birthDate": "1958-02-26 00:00:00", "genres": ["Fiction", "Poetry", "Nonfiction"], "influences": ["Balzac", "Albert Camus", "Georges Perec", "Bret Easton Ellis", "Baudelaire", "Lovecraft", "Sade", "Aldous Huxley", "Arthur Schopenhauer"], "avgRating": 3.72, "reviewsCount": 17701, "ratingsCount": 219228, "about": "Michel Houellebecq (born Michel Thomas), born 26 February 1958 (birth certificate) or 1956 on the French island of R\u00e9union, is a controversial and award-winning French novelist. To admirers he is a writer in the tradition of literary provocation that reaches back to the Marquis de Sade and Baudelaire; to detractors he is a peddler, who writes vulgar sleazy literature to shock. His works though, particularly Atomised, have received high praise from the French literary intelligentsia, with generally positive international critical response, Having written poetry and a biography of the horror writer H. P. Lovecraft, he brought out his first novel Extension du domaine de la lutte in 1994. Les particules \u00e9l\u00e9mentaires followed in 1998 and Platefo Michel Houellebecq (born Michel Thomas), born 26 February 1958 (birth certificate) or 1956 on the French island of R\u00e9union, is a controversial and award-winning French novelist. To admirers he is a writer in the tradition of literary provocation that reaches back to the Marquis de Sade and Baudelaire; to detractors he is a peddler, who writes vulgar sleazy literature to shock. His works though, particularly Atomised, have received high praise from the French literary intelligentsia, with generally positive international critical response, Having written poetry and a biography of the horror writer H. P. Lovecraft, he brought out his first novel Extension du domaine de la lutte in 1994. Les particules \u00e9l\u00e9mentaires followed in 1998 and Plateforme, in 2001. After a disastrous publicity tour for