ia. For more information on her work, visit her website: http://www.rileybanks.net ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/16951538.Tao_Wong", "name": "Tao Wong", "genres": ["Ebooks", "Science Fiction", "Fantasy"], "avgRating": 4.21, "reviewsCount": 3381, "ratingsCount": 70459, "about": "Tao Wong is a Canadian author based in Toronto who is best known for his System Apocalypse post-apocalyptic LitRPG series and A Thousand Li, a Chinese xianxia fantasy series. His work has been released in audio, paperback, hardcover and ebook formats and translated into German, Spanish, Portuguese, Russian and other languages. He was shortlisted for the UK Kindle Storyteller award in 2021 for his work, A Thousand Li: the Second Sect.When he\u2019s not writing and working, he\u2019s practicing martial arts, reading and dreaming up new worlds.Tao became a full-time author in 2019 and is a member of SF Canada, the Science Fiction and Fantasy Writers of America (SFWA) and ALLI."}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/41544.Neil_Sheehan", "name": "Neil Sheehan", "birthDate": "1936-10-27 00:00:00", "genres": ["Nonfiction"], "avgRating": 4.2, "reviewsCount": 665, "ratingsCount": 13593, "about": "Cornelius Mahoney \"Neil\" Sheehan is an American journalist. As a reporter for The New York Times in 1971, Sheehan obtained the classified Pentagon Papers from Daniel Ellsberg. His series of articles revealed a secret U.S. Department of Defense history of the Vietnam War and led to a U.S. Supreme Court case when the United States government attempted to halt publication.He received a Pulitzer Prize and a National Book Award for his 1989 book  A Bright Shining Lie, about the life of Lieutenant Colonel John Paul Vann and the United States involvement in the Vietnam War. Cornelius Mahoney \"Neil\" Sheehan is an American journalist. As a reporter for The New York Times in 1971, Sheehan obtained the classified Pentagon Papers from Daniel Ellsberg. His series of articles revealed a secret U.S. Department of Defense history of the Vietnam War and led to a U.S. Supreme Court case when the United States government attempted to halt publication.He received a Pulitzer Prize and a National Book Award for his 1989 book  A Bright Shining Lie, about the life of Lieutenant Colonel John Paul Vann and the United States involvement in the Vietnam War. ...more"}
