{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/22458.Machado_de_Assis", "name": "Machado de Assis", "birthDate": "1839-06-21 00:00:00", "deathDate": "1908-09-29 00:00:00", "genres": ["Poetry", "Literature & Fiction", "Romance"], "influences": ["William Shakespeare", "Gusta", "Stendhal", " Arthur Schopenhauer", "Laurence Sterne", "E\u00e7a de Queir\u00f3s", "Lu\u00eds Vaz de Cam\u00f5es", "Jonathan Swift", "Gustave Flaubert"], "avgRating": 4.15, "reviewsCount": 7674, "ratingsCount": 117173, "about": "Joaquim Maria Machado de Assis, often known as Machado de Assis, Machado, or Bruxo do Cosme Velho, (June 21, 1839, Rio de Janeiro\u2014September 29, 1908, Rio de Janeiro) was a Brazilian novelist, poet, playwright and short story writer. He is widely regarded as the most important writer of Brazilian literature. However, he did not gain widespread popularity outside Brazil in his own lifetime.Machado's works had a great influence on Brazilian literary schools of the late 19th century and 20th century. Jos\u00e9 Saramago, Carlos Fuentes, Susan Sontag and Harold Bloom are among his admirers and Bloom calls him \"the supreme black literary artist to date.\" Joaquim Maria Machado de Assis, often known as Machado de Assis, Machado, or Bruxo do Cosme Velho, (June 21, 1839, Rio de Janeiro\u2014September 29, 1908, Rio de Janeiro) was a Brazilian novelist, poet, playwright and short story writer. He is widely regarded as the most important writer of Brazilian literature. However, he did not gain widespread popularity outside Brazil in his own lifetime.Machado's works had a great influence on Brazilian literary schools of the late 19th century and 20th century. Jos\u00e9 Saramago, Carlos Fuentes, Susan Sontag and Harold Bloom are among his admirers and Bloom calls him \"the supreme black literary artist to date.\" ...more"}
