{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/8875.Halld_r_Laxness", "name": "Halld\u00f3r Laxness", "birthDate": "1902-04-23 00:00:00", "deathDate": "1998-02-08 00:00:00", "genres": ["Fiction", "Poetry", "Short Stories"], "avgRating": 3.95, "reviewsCount": 3434, "ratingsCount": 27722, "about": "Born Halld\u00f3r Gu\u00f0j\u00f3nsson, he adopted the surname Laxness in honour of Laxnes in Mosfellssveit where he grew up, his family having moved from Reyjav\u00edk in 1905. He published his first novel at the age of only 17, the beginning of a long literary career of more than 60 books, including novels, short stories, poetry, and plays. Confirmed a Catholic in 1923, he later moved away from religion and for a long time was sympathetic to Communist politics, which is evident in his novels World Light and Independent People. In 1955 he was awarded the Nobel Prize for Literature. Born Halld\u00f3r Gu\u00f0j\u00f3nsson, he adopted the surname Laxness in honour of Laxnes in Mosfellssveit where he grew up, his family having moved from Reyjav\u00edk in 1905. He published his first novel at the age of only 17, the beginning of a long literary career of more than 60 books, including novels, short stories, poetry, and plays. Confirmed a Catholic in 1923, he later moved away from religion and for a long time was sympathetic to Communist politics, which is evident in his novels World Light and Independent People. In 1955 he was awarded the Nobel Prize for Literature. ...more"}
