{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/14407836.A_R_Merrydew", "name": "A.R. Merrydew", "genres": ["Science Fiction", "Poetry", "Travel"], "avgRating": 4.25, "reviewsCount": 64, "ratingsCount": 6428, "about": "Born in Dorking Surrey, England, Anthony R Merrydew, was educated at the Andrew Cairns boy\u2019s school, and several colleges in West Sussex. He wrote his first manuscript \u2018Malakoff\u2019, during the early seventies, when he lived and worked in Besancon, France. For reasons best known to him, this remains to this day a work in progress.His first published work, \u2018Our Blue Orange\u2019, was a sci-fi story, which revolved around his fascination for automation, and the world of data. The novel took eight years to complete in his spare time. The second novel in the series, \u2018The Girl with the Porcelain Lips\u2019, was published October 20th, 2023, and has been well received.The third novel in the Science Fiction series, as yet untitled, is planned for publication l Born in Dorking Surrey, England, Anthony R Merrydew, was educated at the Andrew Cairns boy\u2019s school, and several colleges in West Sussex. He wrote his first manuscript \u2018Malakoff\u2019, during the early seventies, when he lived and worked in Besancon, France. For reasons best known to him, this remains to this day a work in progress.His first published work, \u2018Our Blue Orange\u2019, was a sci-fi story, which revolved around his fascination for automation, and the world of data. The novel took eight years to complete in his spare time. The second novel in the series, \u2018The Girl with the Porcelain Lips\u2019, was published October 20th, 2023, and has been well received.The third novel in the Science Fiction series, as yet untitled, is planned for publication later in 2024.Anthony has also published a compilation of his poetry, \u2018From the Pen of an Aquarian\u2019 in 2023. An audio version of his books are available from Audible.com.Anthony currently lives, and travels in his motor home named \u2018Vera\u2019, nearly full time, promoting his writing, poetry and AI Artwork on social media platforms. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/17160667.Stuart_Turton", "name": "Stuart Turton", "avgRating": 3.82, "reviewsCount": 62742, "ratingsCount": 449334, "about": "Stuart lives in London with his amazing wife and two daughters. He drinks lots of tea.What else?\u200bWhen he left university he went travelling for three months and stayed away for five years. Every time his parents asked when he\u2019d be back he told them next week, and meant it.Stuart is not to be trusted. In the nicest possible way. He\u2019s got a degree in English and Philosophy, which makes him excellent at arguing and terrible at choosing degrees. Having trained for no particular career, he has dabbled in most of them. He stocked shelves in a Darwin bookshop, taught English in Shanghai, worked for a technology magazine in London, wrote travel articles in Dubai, and now he\u2019s a freelance journalist. None of this was planned, he just kept getting lo Stuart lives in London with his amazing wife and two daughters. He drinks lots of tea.What else?\u200bWhen he left university he went travelling for three months and stayed away for five years. Every time his parents asked when he\u2019d be back he told them next week, and meant it.Stuart is not to be trusted. In the nicest possible way. He\u2019s got a degree in English and Philosophy, which makes him excellent at arguing and terrible at choosing degrees. Having trained for no particular career, he has dabbled in most of them. He stocked shelves in a Darwin bookshop, taught English in Shanghai, worked for a technology magazine in London, wrote travel articles in Dubai, and now he\u2019s a freelance journalist. None of this was planned, he just kept getting lost on his way to other places.He likes a chat. He likes books. He likes people who write books and people who read books. He doesn\u2019t know how to write a biography, so should probably stop before he tells you about his dreams or something. It was lovely to meet you, though.Stuart's