{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/1159886.Arkady_Strugatsky", "name": "Arkady Strugatsky", "birthDate": "1925-08-28 00:00:00", "deathDate": "1991-10-12 00:00:00", "genres": ["Science Fiction & Fantasy", "Mystery & Thrillers", "Literature & Fiction"], "avgRating": 4.11, "reviewsCount": 9779, "ratingsCount": 153734, "about": "The brothers Arkady Strugatsky [Russian: \u0410\u0440\u043a\u0430\u0434\u0438\u0439 \u0421\u0442\u0440\u0443\u0433\u0430\u0446\u043a\u0438\u0439] and Boris Strugatsky [Russian: \u0411\u043e\u0440\u0438\u0441 \u0421\u0442\u0440\u0443\u0433\u0430\u0446\u043a\u0438\u0439] were Soviet-Russian science fiction authors who collaborated through most of their careers. Arkady Strugatsky was born 25 August 1925 in Batumi; the family later moved to Leningrad. In January 1942, Arkady and his father were evacuated from the Siege of Leningrad, but Arkady was the only survivor in his train car; his father died upon reaching Vologda. Arkady was drafted into the Soviet army in 1943. He trained first at the artillery school in Aktyubinsk and later at the Military Institute of Foreign Languages in Moscow, from which he graduated in 1949 as an interpreter of English and Japanese. He worked as a teacher and interpreter The brothers Arkady Strugatsky [Russian: \u0410\u0440\u043a\u0430\u0434\u0438\u0439 \u0421\u0442\u0440\u0443\u0433\u0430\u0446\u043a\u0438\u0439] and Boris Strugatsky [Russian: \u0411\u043e\u0440\u0438\u0441 \u0421\u0442\u0440\u0443\u0433\u0430\u0446\u043a\u0438\u0439] were Soviet-Russian science fiction authors who collaborated through most of their careers. Arkady Strugatsky was born 25 August 1925 in Batumi; the family later moved to Leningrad. In January 1942, Arkady and his father were evacuated from the Siege of Leningrad, but Arkady was the only survivor in his train car; his father died upon reaching Vologda. Arkady was drafted into the Soviet army in 1943. He trained first at the artillery school in Aktyubinsk and later at the Military Institute of Foreign Languages in Moscow, from which he graduated in 1949 as an interpreter of English and Japanese. He worked as a teacher and interpreter for the military until 1955. In 1955, he began working as an editor and writer. In 1958, he began collaborating with his brother Boris, a collaboration that lasted until Arkady's death on 12 October 1991. Arkady Strugatsky became a member of the Union of Soviet Writers in 1964. In addition to his own writing, he translated Japanese language short stories and novels, as well as some English works with his brother. Source: Wikipedia ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/18715817.Micaiah_Johnson", "name": "Micaiah Johnson", "genres": ["Science Fiction"], "avgRating": 3.95, "reviewsCount": 6037, "ratingsCount": 39496, "about": "Micaiah Johnson was raised in California's Mojave Desert surrounded by trees named Joshua and women who told stories. She received her Bachelor of Arts in creative writing from the University of California, Riverside and her Master of Fine Arts in fiction from Rutgers-Camden. She now studies American Literature at Vanderbilt University where she focuses on critical race theory... and automatons. Micaiah Johnson was raised in California's Mojave Desert surrounded by trees named Joshua and women who told stories. She received her Bachelor of Arts in creative writing from the University of California, Riverside and her Master of Fine Arts in fiction from Rutgers-Camden. She now studies American Literature at Vanderbilt University where she focuses on critical race theory... and automatons. ...more"}
