{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/46293.Nikolas_Schreck", "name": "Nikolas Schreck", "genres": ["Religion & Spirituality", "Nonfiction", "True Crime"], "avgRating": 4.13, "reviewsCount": 137, "ratingsCount": 767, "about": "American writer, musician, film-maker, and spiritual teacher whose work focuses on magic, mysticism, mythology and the macabre. Schreck is married to Zeena Schreck (Formerly LaVey) the daughter of the founder of the Church of Satan, Anton LaveyTogether with his wife he founded the Sethian Liberation Movement and wrote books about sex magic, portrayal of Satan in cinema and Charles Manson.He is also the founder of the gothic-industrial band Radio Werewolf, which was active from 1984 to 1992."}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/14280.Marilyn_Manson", "name": "Marilyn Manson", "birthDate": "1969-01-05 00:00:00", "genres": ["Poetry", "Biographies & Memoirs", "Nonfiction"], "avgRating": 3.83, "reviewsCount": 1616, "ratingsCount": 32056, "about": "Brian Hugh Warner, better known by his stage name Marilyn Manson, is an American musician and artist known for his outrageous stage persona and image as the lead singer of the eponymous band. His stage name was formed from the names of actress Marilyn Monroe and convicted murderer Charles Manson. In 2004, the band's hit \"mOBSCENE\" was nominated for a Grammy Award for \"Best Metal Performance\". Brian Hugh Warner, better known by his stage name Marilyn Manson, is an American musician and artist known for his outrageous stage persona and image as the lead singer of the eponymous band. His stage name was formed from the names of actress Marilyn Monroe and convicted murderer Charles Manson. In 2004, the band's hit \"mOBSCENE\" was nominated for a Grammy Award for \"Best Metal Performance\". ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/771577.H_Hesketh_Prichard", "name": "H. Hesketh-Prichard", "birthDate": "1876-11-17 00:00:00", "deathDate": "1922-06-14 00:00:00", "genres": ["Mystery & Thrillers", "Travel", "Outdoors & Nature"], "avgRating": 3.7, "reviewsCount": 171, "ratingsCount": 1359, "about": "See also H. Heron.Major Hesketh Vernon Prichard, later Hesketh-Prichard, DSO, MC, FRGS, FZS (17 November 1876 \u2013 14 June 1922) was an explorer, adventurer, big-game hunter and marksman who made a significant contribution to sniping practice within the British Army during the First World War. Concerned not only with improving the quality of marksmanship, the measures he introduced to counter the threat of German snipers were credited by a contemporary with saving the lives of over 3,500 Allied soldiers.During his lifetime, he also explored territory never seen before, played cricket at first-class level, including on overseas tours, wrote short stories and novels (one of which was turned into a Douglas Fairbanks film) and was a successful new See also H. Heron.Major Hesketh Vernon Prichard, later Hesketh-Prichard, DSO, MC, FRGS, FZS (17 November 1876 \u2013 14 June 1922) was an explorer, adventurer, big-game hunter and marksman who made a significant contribution to sniping practice within the British Army during the First World War. Concerned not only with improving the quality of marksmanship, the measures he introduced to counter the threat of German snipers were credited by a contemporary with saving the lives of over 3,500 Allied soldiers.During his lifetime, he also explored territory never seen before, played cricket at first-class level, including on overseas tours, wrote short stories and novels (one of which was turned into a Douglas Fairbanks film) and was a successful newspaper correspondent and travel writer. His many activities brought him into the highest social and professional circles. Despite a lifetime's passion for shooting, he was an active campaigner for animal welfare and succeeded in seeing legal measures introduced for their protection. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/26359.Leonora_Carrington", "name": "Leonora Carrington", "birthDate": "1917-04-06 00:00:00", "deathDate": "2011-05-25 00:00:00", "genres": ["Literature & Fiction", "Short Stories", "Arts & Photography"], "influences": ["Max Ernst", "Remedios Varo"], "avgRating": 3.98, "reviewsCount": 2963, "ratingsCount": 20325, "about": "Leonora Carrington was an English-born Mexican artist, surrealist painter, and novelist. She lived most of her adult life in Mexico City, and was one of the last surviving participants in the Surrealist movement of the 1930s. Carrington was also a founding member of the Women\u2019s Liberation Movement in Mexico during the 1970s."}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/130421.Florence_Marryat", "name": "Florence Marryat", "birthDate": "1833-07-09 00:00:00", "deathDate": "1899-10-27 00:00:00", "genres": ["Science Fiction & Fantasy", "Nonfiction"], "avgRating": 3.7, "reviewsCount": 222, "ratingsCount": 1391, "about": "British author and actress, daughter of author Capt. Frederick Marryat (Children of the The New Forest), particularly known for her sensational novels and her involvement with several celebrated spiritual mediums of the late nineteenth century. Her works include There is No Death (1891) and The Spirit World (1894).Marryat's parents separated when she was young; her childhood was divided between her parents' residences, where she was privately educated.Shortly before her 21st birthday, she wed Thomas Ross Church, an officer in the Madras staff corps of the British Army in India; they spent the first seven years of their married life traveling India extensively before she returned to England in 1860. They had eight children but divorced in 18 British author and actress, daughter of author Capt. Frederick Marryat (Children of the The New Forest), particularly known for her sensational novels and her involvement with several celebrated spiritual mediums of the late nineteenth century. Her works include There is No Death (1891) and The Spirit World (1894).Marryat's parents separated when she was young; her childhood was divided between her parents' residences, where she was privately educated.Shortly before her 21st birthday, she wed Thomas Ross Church, an officer in the Madras staff corps of the British Army in India; they spent the first seven years of their married life traveling India extensively before she returned to England in 1860. They had eight children but divorced in 1879; later that year, Marryat wed Colonel Francis Lean. At the age of 43, Marryat entered the stage, taking a role in a drama she had written, Her World Against a Lie, in 1881. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/7134334.Eric_LaRocca", "name": "Eric LaRocca", "genres": ["Gay and Lesbian", "Fantasy", "Horror"], "avgRating": 3.14, "reviewsCount": 22444, "ratingsCount": 86242, "about": "Eric LaRocca (he/they) is a 2x Bram Stoker Award\u00ae finalist and Splatterpunk Award winner. His notable works include Things Have Gotten Worse Since We Last Spoke, Everything the Darkness Eats, The Trees Grew Because I Bled There: Collected Stories, and You\u2019ve Lost a Lot of Blood. His upcoming novel, At Dark, I Become Loathsome, will be published by Blackstone Publishing in January 2025 and has already been optioned for film by The Walking Dead star Norman Reedus."}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/175282.Robert_Marasco", "name": "Robert Marasco", "birthDate": "1936-09-22 00:00:00", "deathDate": "1998-12-10 00:00:00", "genres": ["Horror"], "avgRating": 3.79, "reviewsCount": 974, "ratingsCount": 8701, "about": "Robert Marasco was born in the Bronx in 1936 and educated at Regis High School in Manhattan and Fordham University. A classical scholar, Marasco taught at Regis before turning to writing, with Child\u2019s Play, an eerie melodrama about incidents of evil at a Catholic boys\u2019 school. The play was a surprise success in 1970, running for 343 performances on Broadway and earning a Tony Award nomination for best play of the year, and was adapted for a 1972 film.Marasco also wrote two novels: Burnt Offerings (1973) and Parlor Games (1979). Burnt Offerings was a bestseller and spawned a 1976 film adaptation directed by Dan Curtis and starring Oliver Reed, Karen Black, and Bette Davis.Marasco died of lung cancer in 1998."}
