{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/915500.Matthew_Desmond", "name": "Matthew Desmond", "genres": ["Contemporary", "Nonfiction"], "avgRating": 4.42, "reviewsCount": 17372, "ratingsCount": 137662, "about": "Matthew Desmond is social scientist and urban ethnographer. He is the Maurice P. During Professor of Sociology and the Director of the Eviction Lab at Princeton University. He is also a Contributing Writer for The New York Times Magazine.Desmond is the author of over fifty academic studies and several books, including \"Evicted: Poverty and Profit in the American City,\" which won the Pulitzer Prize for General Nonfiction, National Book Critics Circle Award, Carnegie Medal, and PEN / John Kenneth Galbraith Award for Nonfiction.\"Evicted\" was listed as one of the Best Books of 2016 by The New York Times, New Yorker, Washington Post, National Public Radio, and several other outlets. It has been named one of the Best 50 Nonfiction Books of the La Matthew Desmond is social scientist and urban ethnographer. He is the Maurice P. During Professor of Sociology and the Director of the Eviction Lab at Princeton University. He is also a Contributing Writer for The New York Times Magazine.Desmond is the author of over fifty academic studies and several books, including \"Evicted: Poverty and Profit in the American City,\" which won the Pulitzer Prize for General Nonfiction, National Book Critics Circle Award, Carnegie Medal, and PEN / John Kenneth Galbraith Award for Nonfiction.\"Evicted\" was listed as one of the Best Books of 2016 by The New York Times, New Yorker, Washington Post, National Public Radio, and several other outlets. It has been named one of the Best 50 Nonfiction Books of the Last 100 Years and was included in the 100 Best Social Policy Books of All Time.Desmond's research and reporting focuses on American poverty and public policy. He is the recipient of a MacArthur Fellowship, the American Bar Association\u2019s Silver Gavel Award, and is an elected member of the American Philosophical Society. He has been listed among the Politico 50, as one of \u201cfifty people across the country who are most influencing the national political debate.\u201d ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/10442.Robert_Cormier", "name": "Robert Cormier", "birthDate": "1925-01-17 00:00:00", "deathDate": "2000-11-02 00:00:00", "genres": ["Young Adult", "Literature & Fiction", "Thriller"], "avgRating": 3.59, "reviewsCount": 8343, "ratingsCount": 89892, "about": "Robert Edmund Cormier (January 17, 1925\u2013November 2, 2000) was an American author, columnist and reporter, known for his deeply pessimistic, downbeat literature. His most popular works include I Am the Cheese, After the First Death, We All Fall Down and The Chocolate War, all of which have won awards. The Chocolate War was challenged in multiple libraries. His books often are concerned with themes such as abuse, mental illness, violence, revenge, betrayal and conspiracy. In most of his novels, the protagonists do not win."}
