{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/55727.Jonathan_Haidt", "name": "Jonathan Haidt", "birthDate": "1963-10-19 00:00:00", "genres": ["Science", "Social Sciences", "Psychology"], "influences": ["Max Weber", "David Hume", "Charles Darwin", "\u00c9mile Durkheim"], "avgRating": 4.21, "reviewsCount": 15574, "ratingsCount": 152354, "about": "Jonathan Haidt is the Thomas Cooley Professor of Ethical Leadership at New York University\u2019s Stern School of Business. He obtained his PhD in social psychology from the University of Pennsylvania in 1992 and taught at the University of Virginia for sixteen years. His research focuses on moral and political psychology, as described in his book The Righteous Mind. His latest book, The Anxious Generation, is a direct continuation of the themes explored in The Coddling of the American Mind (written with Greg Lukianoff). He writes the After Babel Substack."}
