{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/269069.Michelle_Moran", "name": "Michelle    Moran", "genres": ["Fiction", "Historical Fiction"], "avgRating": 4.07, "reviewsCount": 12919, "ratingsCount": 140844, "about": "Librarian Note: There is more than one author in the GoodReads database with this name. See this thread for more information. Michelle Moran is the internationally bestselling author of eight historical novels. A native of southern California, she attended Pomona College, then earned a Masters Degree from the Claremont Graduate University. During her six years as a public high school teacher, she used her summers to travel around the world, and it was her experiences as a volunteer on archaeological digs that inspired her to write historical fiction. Her novels, translated into more than twenty languages, include Nefertiti, The Heretic Queen, Cleopatra\u2019s Daughter, Madame Tussaud, The Second Empress, Rebel Queen, Mata Hari, and Maria. A freq Librarian Note: There is more than one author in the GoodReads database with this name. See this thread for more information. Michelle Moran is the internationally bestselling author of eight historical novels. A native of southern California, she attended Pomona College, then earned a Masters Degree from the Claremont Graduate University. During her six years as a public high school teacher, she used her summers to travel around the world, and it was her experiences as a volunteer on archaeological digs that inspired her to write historical fiction. Her novels, translated into more than twenty languages, include Nefertiti, The Heretic Queen, Cleopatra\u2019s Daughter, Madame Tussaud, The Second Empress, Rebel Queen, Mata Hari, and Maria. A frequent traveler, she currently lives with her family in England, where she is researching her ninth book. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/17992633.Daniel_Mangena", "name": "Daniel Mangena", "genres": ["Business", "Spirituality", "Self Help"], "avgRating": 4.33, "reviewsCount": 40, "ratingsCount": 6248, "about": "By his late twenties, Daniel Mangena was ready to give up. He had built and lost two multi-million dollar fortunes, but with everything stripped from him a second time and the shattering late diagnosis of Asperger\u2019s syndrome; he felt that there was nothing left for him but failure. In seeking a way to end his life, it was the fear of failing to do so effectively that lead him to understand he was central to every aspect of his life. This realisation gave him back his power. The methodology that he created as a result, ultimately led him to the creation of Stepping Beyond Intention his first best-selling book.Daniel followed this up with three more best-selling books: From Time to Time, The Dreamer\u2019s Manifesto and The Money Game: A Wealth Ma By his late twenties, Daniel Mangena was ready to give up. He had built and lost two multi-million dollar fortunes, but with everything stripped from him a second time and the shattering late diagnosis of Asperger\u2019s syndrome; he felt that there was nothing left for him but failure. In seeking a way to end his life, it was the fear of failing to do so effectively that lead him to understand he was central to every aspect of his life. This realisation gave him back his power. The methodology that he created as a result, ultimately led him to the creation of Stepping Beyond Intention his first best-selling book.Daniel followed this up with three more best-selling books: From Time to Time, The Dreamer\u2019s Manifesto and The Money Game: A Wealth Manifestation Guide. These books have offered countless others the opportunity to learn from the years of personal experience and hardship that Daniel has gone through, as well as the hundreds of thousands of dollars he has spent on personal development coaching. They offer incredible value, insight and proven methods for wealth creation, time management and any other area of your life that you want to improve. Today Daniel lives his ultimate, dream life in Cabo, Mexico with his young family. He speaks regularly, offers group coaching and one-to-one sessions. He is a guest contributor to Entrepreneur Magazine, Brainz Magazine, The Good Men Project and Elephant Journal to name but a few. His ongoing mission is to empower people and give them what they need, in order to choose a life of abundance. He is passionate and dedicated to enabling others to realise their own, unique dream life - using the very tools that have enabled him to do just that. Through his powerful speaking engagements, live coaching, retreats and writing: Daniel continues to create massive change and results for his clients. He is a shining example of how we can all choose to start again, any time that we want to and no matter how hopeless our situation may seem. ...more"}
