{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/88550.Joseph_Boyden", "name": "Joseph Boyden", "birthDate": "1966-10-31 00:00:00", "genres": ["Literature & Fiction", "Short Stories"], "avgRating": 4.22, "reviewsCount": 6247, "ratingsCount": 66917, "about": "Joseph Boyden is a Canadian novelist and short story writer.He grew up in Willowdale, North York, Ontario and attended the Jesuit-run Brebeuf College School. Boyden's father Raymond Wilfrid Boyden was a medical officer renowned for his bravery, who was awarded the Distinguished Service Order and was the highest-decorated medical officer of World War II.Boyden, of Irish, Scottish and M\u00e9tis heritage, writes about First Nations heritage and culture. Three Day Road, a novel about two Cree soldiers serving in the Canadian military during World War I, is inspired by Ojibwa Francis Pegahmagabow, the legendary First World War sniper. Boyden's second novel, Through Black Spruce follows the story of Will, son of one of the characters in Three Day Roa Joseph Boyden is a Canadian novelist and short story writer.He grew up in Willowdale, North York, Ontario and attended the Jesuit-run Brebeuf College School. Boyden's father Raymond Wilfrid Boyden was a medical officer renowned for his bravery, who was awarded the Distinguished Service Order and was the highest-decorated medical officer of World War II.Boyden, of Irish, Scottish and M\u00e9tis heritage, writes about First Nations heritage and culture. Three Day Road, a novel about two Cree soldiers serving in the Canadian military during World War I, is inspired by Ojibwa Francis Pegahmagabow, the legendary First World War sniper. Boyden's second novel, Through Black Spruce follows the story of Will, son of one of the characters in Three Day Road. He has indicated in interviews that the titles are part of a planned trilogy, the third of which is forthcoming.He studied creative writing at York University and the University of New Orleans, and subsequently taught in the Abor