{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/36378.Amin_Maalouf", "name": "Amin Maalouf", "genres": ["Literature & Fiction", "Nonfiction", "History"], "influences": ["Albert Camus", "Thomas Mann", "Marguerite Y", "Stefan Zweig", "L\u00e9on Tolsto\u00ef", "Marguerite Yourcenar", "Charles Dickens", "Omar Khayy\u00e1m"], "avgRating": 4.07, "reviewsCount": 11243, "ratingsCount": 117317, "about": "Amin Maalouf (Arabic: \u0623\u0645\u064a\u0646 \u0645\u0639\u0644\u0648\u0641; alternate spelling Amin Maluf) is a Lebanese journalist and novelist. He writes and publishes primarily in French.Most of Maalouf's books have a historical setting, and like Umberto Eco, Orhan Pamuk, and Arturo P\u00e9rez-Reverte, Maalouf mixes fascinating historical facts with fantasy and philosophical ideas. In an interview Maalouf has said that his role as a writer is to create \"positive myths\". Maalouf's works, written with the skill of a master storyteller, offer a sensitive view of the values and attitudes of different cultures in the Middle East, Africa and Mediterranean world. Amin Maalouf (Arabic: \u0623\u0645\u064a\u0646 \u0645\u0639\u0644\u0648\u0641; alternate spelling Amin Maluf) is a Lebanese journalist and novelist. He writes and publishes primarily in French.Most of Maalouf's books have a historical setting, and like Umberto Eco, Orhan Pamuk, and Arturo P\u00e9rez-Reverte, Maalouf mixes fascinating historical facts with fantasy and philosophical ideas. In an interview Maalouf has said that his role as a writer is to create \"positive myths\". Maalouf's works, written with the skill of a master storyteller, offer a sensitive view of the values and attitudes of different cultures in the Middle East, Africa and Mediterranean world. ...more"}
