in my sleep. I like waking up early to sit at the typewriter and warm my hands on a cup of Sanka. When the sun comes up, I make himself toast with butter and English marmalade and get depressed looking at my empty plate with the crumbs on it, like the world is nothing but toast and marmalade and crumbs. That\u2019s when I\u2019ll open the fridge and have a look see. I usually end up closing the door without taking anything out but might come back later and open the door again, or might not. And the J stands for Johnny.\"Jupes also likes , as the English say, taking the piss. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/7172051.Stevie_Turner", "name": "Stevie Turner", "genres": ["Humor and Comedy", "Contemporary", "Suspense"], "avgRating": 4.03, "reviewsCount": 422, "ratingsCount": 1876, "about": "Stevie Turner is a British author of suspense, paranormal, women's fiction family dramas, and darkly humorous novels. She has also branched out into the world of audio books, screenplays, and translations. Her third novel 'A House Without Windows' gained the attention of a New York media production company in December 2017, and her screenplay 'For the Sake of a Child' won Silver in the 2017 Depth of Field International Film Festival. Her novella 'Finding David' was a quarter-finalist in the 2019 ScreenCraft Cinematic Short Story Competition. https://writers.coverfly.com/profile/... Her novella 'Scam!' won the Electric Eclectic Novella Fiction Prize for 2020: https://electriceclecticsblog.wordpre... Her novel 'His Ladyship' made the finals a Stevie Turner is a British author of suspense, paranormal, women's fiction family dramas, and darkly humorous novels. She has also branched out into the world of audio books, screenplays, and translations. Her third novel 'A House Without Windows' gained the attention of a New York media production company in December 2017, and her screenplay 'For the Sake of a Child' won Silver in the 2017 Depth of Field International Film Festival. Her novella 'Finding David' was a quarter-finalist in the 2019 ScreenCraft Cinematic Short Story Competition. https://writers.coverfly.com/profile/... Her novella 'Scam!' won the Electric Eclectic Novella Fiction Prize for 2020: https://electriceclecticsblog.wordpre... Her novel 'His Ladyship' made the finals and Longlist of the 2021 Page Turner Award, and her new manuscript 'Falling' reached the finals of the 2022 Page Turner Award. Her latest unpublished manuscript 'Tina's Diary: 1997' also reached the finals of the 2023 Page Turner Writing Award.To quote reader Roberta Bade