{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/7159563.Widad_Akreyi", "name": "Widad Akreyi", "genres": ["Science", "Biography", "History"], "avgRating": 4.4, "reviewsCount": 30, "ratingsCount": 701, "about": "Multiple award-winner Widad Akreyi is the author of a number of books. Her series, \u201cTHE VIKING'S KURDISH LOVE,\u201d chronicles an original story which may make you view our shared history with new eyes. Her memoir, \u201cTHE DAUGHTER OF KURDLAND,\u201d weaves together the personal and political events that have shaped her, while exploring what makes us the people we are. \u201cANATOMY OF COVID CALAMITY,\u201d combines recent pandemic research with critical reflection.Her awards include Pacem in Terris Peace and Freedom Award, International Woman Harmony Award, Davenport Mayor Medal, International Pfeffer Peace Award, and Prize for bridging gaps between cultures.Although born in Kurdland, her heart resides in several western cities scattered across vast continents. Multiple award-winner Widad Akreyi is the author of a number of books. Her series, \u201cTHE VIKING'S KURDISH LOVE,\u201d chronicles an original story which may make you view our shared history with new eyes. Her memoir, \u201cTHE DAUGHTER OF KURDLAND,\u201d weaves together the personal and political events that have shaped her, while exploring what makes us the people we are. \u201cANATOMY OF COVID CALAMITY,\u201d combines recent pandemic research with critical reflection.Her awards include Pacem in Terris Peace and Freedom Award, International Woman Harmony Award, Davenport Mayor Medal, International Pfeffer Peace Award, and Prize for bridging gaps between cultures.Although born in Kurdland, her heart resides in several western cities scattered across vast continents.Widad has donated her manuscripts to charity and receives no royalties for any books published. All proceeds from the sale of her books go to charitable causes.You can reach her:http://www.widad.orghttps://twitter.com/DrWidad_Aht