{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/6452053.Kimberly_McCreight", "name": "Kimberly McCreight", "birthDate": "0001-09-20 00:00:00", "genres": ["Literature & Fiction", "Mystery & Thrillers"], "avgRating": 3.81, "reviewsCount": 25340, "ratingsCount": 251118, "about": "Kimberly McCreight is the New York Times bestselling author of several literary thrillers including RECONSTRUCTING AMELIA, A GOOD MARRIAGE and FRIENDS LIKE THESE. Her next book LIKE MOTHER, LIKE DAUGHTER (Knopf) is forthcoming in July 2024. She has been nominated for the Edgar, Anthony and Alex awards and her books have been translated into more than twenty languages. She attended Vassar College and graduated cum laude from the University of Pennsylvania Law School. She lives in Brooklyn with her two teenaged daughters. You can find her on Instagram and Facebook and at kimberlymccreight.com"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/1779542.Mrs_Henry_Wood", "name": "Mrs. Henry Wood", "birthDate": "1814-01-17 00:00:00", "deathDate": "1887-02-10 00:00:00", "genres": ["Classics"], "avgRating": 3.77, "reviewsCount": 700, "ratingsCount": 7467, "about": "Ellen Wood (n\u00e9e Price) was an English novelist, better known as \"Mrs Henry Wood\". She wrote over 30 novels, many of which (especially East Lynne), enjoyed remarkable popularity. Among the best known of her stories are Danesbury House, Oswald Cray, Mrs. Halliburton's Troubles, The Channings, Lord Oakburn's Daughters and The Shadow of Ashlydyat. For many years, she worked as the proprietor and editor of the Argosy. Ellen Wood (n\u00e9e Price) was an English novelist, better known as \"Mrs Henry Wood\". She wrote over 30 novels, many of which (especially East Lynne), enjoyed remarkable popularity. Among the best known of her stories are Danesbury House, Oswald Cray, Mrs. Halliburton's Troubles, The Channings, Lord Oakburn's Daughters and The Shadow of Ashlydyat. For many years, she worked as the proprietor and editor of the Argosy. ...more"}
