{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/51484.Paul_Zindel", "name": "Paul Zindel", "birthDate": "1936-05-15 00:00:00", "deathDate": "2003-03-27 00:00:00", "genres": ["Young Adult", "Literature & Fiction"], "avgRating": 3.65, "reviewsCount": 2925, "ratingsCount": 48402, "about": "Paul Zindel was an American author, playwright and educator.In 1964, he wrote The Effect of Gamma Rays on Man-in-the-Moon Marigolds, his first and most successful play. The play ran off-Broadway in 1970, and on Broadway in 1971. It won the 1971 Pulitzer Prize for Drama. It was also made into a 1972 movie by 20th Century Fox. Charlotte Zolotow, then a vice-president at Harper &amp; Row (now Harper-Collins) contacted him to writing for her book label. Zindel wrote 39 books, all of them aimed at children or young adults. Many of these were set in his home town of Staten Island, New York. They tended to be semi-autobiographical, focusing on teenage misfits with abusive or neglectful parents. Despite the often dark subject matter of his books, which Paul Zindel was an American author, playwright and educator.In 1964, he wrote The Effect of Gamma Rays on Man-in-the-Moon Marigolds, his first and most successful play. The play ran off-Broadway in 1970, and on Broadway in 1971. It won the 1971 Pulitzer Prize for Drama. It was also made into a 1972 movie by 20th Century Fox. Charlotte Zolotow, then a vice-president at Harper &amp; Row (now Harper-Collins) contacted him to writing for her book label. Zindel wrote 39 books, all of them aimed at children or young adults. Many of these were set in his home town of Staten Island, New York. They tended to be semi-autobiographical, focusing on teenage misfits with abusive or neglectful parents. Despite the often dark subject matter of his books, which deal with loneliness, loss, and the effects of abuse, they are also filled with humor. Many of his novels have wacky titles, such as My Darling, My Hamburger, or Confessions of A Teenage Baboon.The Pigman, first published in 1968, is widely taught in American schools, and also made it on to the list of most frequently banned books in America in the 1990s, because of what some deem offensive language. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/17671937.Adalyn_Grace", "name": "Adalyn  Grace", "avgRating": 3.96, "reviewsCount": 30207, "ratingsCount": 169845, "about": "Adalyn Grace is the #1 New York Times, USA Today, Wall Street Journal, International, and Indiebound bestselling author of Belladonna and the All the Stars and Teeth duology.Prior to becoming an author, Adalyn spent several years working in live theatre and studied storytelling as an intern on Nickelodeon Animation\u2019s popular series The Legend of Korra. Local to San Diego, Adalyn spends her non-writing days by watching too much anime, and by playing video games with her two dorky dogs."}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/10810.Derek_Prince", "name": "Derek Prince", "birthDate": "1915-08-14 00:00:00", "deathDate": "2003-09-24 00:00:00", "genres": ["Christian", "Religion", "Spirituality"], "avgRating": 4.45, "reviewsCount": 1330, "ratingsCount": 13447, "about": "Derek Prince (1915-2003), was an International Bible teacher and founder of Derek Prince Ministries International, wrote more than fifty books. He was born in India of British parents. Educated as a scholar of Greek and Latin at Eton College and Cambridge University, England, he held a Fellowship in Ancient and Modern Philosophy at King\u2019s College. He also studied Hebrew and Aramaic, at Cambridge University and the Hebrew University in Jerusalem. His daily radio broadcast, Derek Prince Legacy Radio, still reaches listeners around the world."}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/18914293.Micah_Nemerever", "name": "Micah Nemerever", "genres": ["Fiction", "Gay and Lesbian", "Historical Fiction"], "avgRating": 3.98, "reviewsCount": 4920, "ratingsCount": 18627, "about": "Micah Nemerever was trained as an art historian. He wrote his master\u2019s thesis on queer identity and gender anxiety in the art of the Weimar Republic. He is an avid home chef and amateur historian of queer cinema.After studying in rural Connecticut and Austin, Texas, he now resides in the Pacific Northwest."}
