t was chosen by the American Library Association for its Best Books for Young Adults list, and translated into more than two dozen languages for distribution in over 30 countries. Simon &amp; Schuster released a special 15th anniversary edition in December of \u201914. Pay It Forward: Young Readers Edition, an age-appropriate edited edition of the original novel, was released by Simon &amp; Schuster in August of \u201814. It is suitable for children as young as eight.You can learn much more about Catherine at www.catherineryanhyde.com ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/50314.James_Hogg", "name": "James Hogg", "birthDate": "1770-01-01 00:00:00", "deathDate": "1835-11-21 00:00:00", "genres": ["Poetry", "Historical Fiction", "Short Stories"], "influences": ["Edmund Spe", "Edmund Spenser", "Walter Scott", "Samuel Johnson", "Thomas Pennant", "Robert Burns"], "avgRating": 3.7, "reviewsCount": 1096, "ratingsCount": 14392, "about": "James Hogg was a Scottish poet, novelist and essayist who wrote in Scots and English. As a young man he worked as a shepherd and farmhand, and was largely self-educated through reading. He was a friend of many of the great writers of his day, including Sir  Walter Scott, of whom he later wrote an unauthorized biography. He became widely known as the \"Ettrick Shepherd\", a nickname under which some of his works were published, and the character name he was given in the widely read series 'Noctes Ambrosianae', published in Blackwood's Magazine. He is best known today for his novel The Private Memoirs and Confessions of a Justified Sinner. His other works include the long poem The Queen's Wake, his collection of songs Jacobite Reliques, and the James Hogg was a Scottish poet, novelist and essayist who wrote in Scots and English. As a young man he worked as a shepherd and farmhand, and was largely self-educated through reading. He was a friend of many of the great writers of his day, including Sir  Walter Scott, of whom he later wrote an unauthorized biography. He became widely known as the \"Ettrick Shepherd\", a nickname under which some of his works were published, and the character name he was given in the widely read series 'Noctes Ambrosianae', published in Blackwood's Magazine. He is best known today for his novel The Private Memoirs and Confessions of a Justified Sinner. His other works include the long poem The Queen's Wake, his collection of songs Jacobite Reliques, and the novels The Three Perils of Man, The Three Perils of Woman, and The Brownie of Bodsbe