{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/61124.Chetan_Bhagat", "name": "Chetan Bhagat", "birthDate": "1974-04-22 00:00:00", "genres": ["Fiction", "Contemporary", "Self Help"], "avgRating": 3.22, "reviewsCount": 21283, "ratingsCount": 533600, "about": "Chetan Bhagat writes op-ed columns for English and Hindi newspapers, including Times of India and Dainik Bhaskar, focusing on youth and issues based on national development. Bhagat is also a motivational speaker and has given talks in leading MNCs and other institutions. He quit his international investment banking career in 2009, to devote his entire time to writing. In 2008, The New York Times called Bhagat \"the biggest selling English language novelist in India\u2019s history\". Bhagat, a graduate of Indian Institute of Technology (IIT) Delhi and IIM Ahmedabad, is seen more as a youth icon than as an author. Chetan Bhagat writes op-ed columns for English and Hindi newspapers, including Times of India and Dainik Bhaskar, focusing on youth and issues based on national development. Bhagat is also a motivational speaker and has given talks in leading MNCs and other institutions. He quit his international investment banking career in 2009, to devote his entire time to writing. In 2008, The New York Times called Bhagat \"the biggest selling English language novelist in India\u2019s history\". Bhagat, a graduate of Indian Institute of Technology (IIT) Delhi and IIM Ahmedabad, is seen more as a youth icon than as an author. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/9640.Karen_Cushman", "name": "Karen Cushman", "birthDate": "0001-10-04 00:00:00", "genres": ["Historical Fiction", "Literature & Fiction", "Children's Books"], "avgRating": 3.72, "reviewsCount": 6440, "ratingsCount": 100349, "about": "Karen Cushman was born in Chicago, Illinois. She entered Stanford University on a scholarship in 1959 and graduated with degrees in Greek and English. She later earned master\u2019s degrees in human behavior and museum studies.For eleven years she was an adjunct professor in the Museum Studies Department at John F. Kennedy University before resigning in 1996 to write full-time. She lives on Vashon Island, Washington with her husband, Philip.(source: http://karencushman.com/about/bio.html &amp; http://www.arnenixoncenter.org/findin...) Karen Cushman was born in Chicago, Illinois. She entered Stanford University on a scholarship in 1959 and graduated with degrees in Greek and English. She later earned master\u2019s degrees in human behavior and museum studies.For eleven years she was an adjunct professor in the Museum Studies Department at John F. Kennedy University before resigning in 1996 to write full-time. She lives on Vashon Island, Washington with her husband, Philip.(source: http://karencushman.com/about/bio.html &amp; http://www.arnenixoncenter.org/findin...) ...more"}
