her\u2019s cult film, \u201cHieronymus Merkin,\u201dwon the Best Original Screenplay award from The Writers Guild of Great Britain. His racially charged movie, \u201cWatermelon Man,\u201dshook up the film critics no small end.He still feels most at home with novels, in that no one can change as much as a comma without his approval\u2014a condition that every writer savors but very few achieve. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/227832.William_H_Hallahan", "name": "William H. Hallahan", "birthDate": "1925-12-12 00:00:00", "deathDate": "2018-08-21 00:00:00", "genres": ["Mystery & Thrillers", "History"], "avgRating": 3.67, "reviewsCount": 180, "ratingsCount": 981, "about": "William Henry Hallahan was an American writer, best known for his two occult novels, The Search for Joseph Tully and The Keeper of the Children.Mr. Hallahan started in the advertising business and stayed in the business for most of his adult life, but in 1971 with the publication of his first novel, The Dead of Winter, he began a second career as a writer. Over the next seventeen years he would write eight novels. In the 1990's he switched from fiction to non-fiction. Mr. Hallahan served in the United States Navy as a radio operator during World War II He is survived by his daughter and a brother. He passed away at the age of 92. William Henry Hallahan was an American writer, best known for his two occult novels, The Search for Joseph Tully and The Keeper of the Children.Mr. Hallahan started in the advertising business and stayed in the business for most of his adult life, but in 1971 with the publication of his first novel, The Dead of Winter, he began a second career as a writer. Over the next seventeen years he would write eight novels. In the 1990's he switched from fiction to non-fiction. Mr. Hallahan served in the United States Navy as a radio operator during World War II He is survived by his daughter and a brother. He passed away at the age of 92. ...more"}
