{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/6916215.Karena_Marie", "name": "Karena Marie", "birthDate": "0001-09-15 00:00:00", "genres": ["Ebooks", "Fiction", "Fantasy"], "avgRating": 4.35, "reviewsCount": 65, "ratingsCount": 292, "about": "Karena Marie is an award winning author of erotica. Her debut novel, The Happy Spinster, was received with mixed reviews as the twists and turns her readers now expect, left some shocked by the ending. Some readers were upset and considered the ending to be a cliff-hanger. Next published was The Date, where Tawny's adventures continued and concluded in The Choice. All three are now available in the box set, The Happy Spinster Trilogy. Readers love her well written, scorching hot and spicy sex scenes, realistic dialogues that feature strong, sassy, confident women and their hot alpha males in the thrilling biker love story, Lukas, The Barmaid who takes a second chance at love and the award winning Montreal Escort. A prolific writer, several Karena Marie is an award winning author of erotica. Her debut novel, The Happy Spinster, was received with mixed reviews as the twists and turns her readers now expect, left some shocked by the ending. Some readers were upset and considered the ending to be a cliff-hanger. Next published was The Date, where Tawny's adventures continued and concluded in The Choice. All three are now available in the box set, The Happy Spinster Trilogy. Readers love her well written, scorching hot and spicy sex scenes, realistic dialogues that feature strong, sassy, confident women and their hot alpha males in the thrilling biker love story, Lukas, The Barmaid who takes a second chance at love and the award winning Montreal Escort. A prolific writer, several of Karena's stories are currently in various stages of post-production. Look for new releases in 2016 featuring a hunky firefighter and the ladies from Montreal Escort return to discuss some of their hottest adventures in 'Pillow Talk'. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/6263.Jun_ichir_Tanizaki", "name": "Jun'ichir\u014d Tanizaki", "birthDate": "1886-07-24 00:00:00", "deathDate": "1965-07-30 00:00:00", "genres": ["Literature & Fiction", "Essays", "Nonfiction"], "influences": ["Wilde", "Sade", "Baudelaire", "Poe"], "avgRating": 3.83, "reviewsCount": 9322, "ratingsCount": 81233, "about": "Jun'ichir\u014d Tanizaki (\u8c37\u5d0e \u6f64\u4e00\u90ce) was a Japanese author, and one of the major writers of modern Japanese literature, perhaps the most popular Japanese novelist after Natsume S\u014dseki. Some of his works present a rather shocking world of sexuality and destructive erotic obsessions; others, less sensational, subtly portray the dynamics of family life in the context of the rapid changes in 20th-century Japanese society. Frequently his stories are narrated in the context of a search for cultural identity in which constructions of \"the West\" and \"Japanese tradition\" are juxtaposed. The results are complex, ironic, demure, and provocative. Jun'ichir\u014d Tanizaki (\u8c37\u5d0e \u6f64\u4e00\u90ce) was a Japanese author, and one of the major writers of modern Japanese literature, perhaps the most popular Japanese novelist after Natsume S\u014dseki. Some of his works present a rather shocking world of sexuality and destructive erotic obsessions; others, less sensational, subtly portray the dynamics of family life in the context of the rapid changes in 20th-century Japanese society. Frequently his stories are narrated in the context of a search for cultural identity in which constructions of \"the West\" and \"Japanese tradition\" are juxtaposed. The results are complex, ironic, demure, and provocative. ...more"}
