{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/82467.Clare_B_Dunkle", "name": "Clare B. Dunkle", "birthDate": "1964-06-11 00:00:00", "genres": ["Science Fiction & Fantasy"], "avgRating": 3.96, "reviewsCount": 2714, "ratingsCount": 29061, "about": "I was born Clare Buckalew in Fort Worth, Texas, and grew up in Denton, Texas, a city north of Dallas. I earned my B.A. in Russian with a minor in Latin from Trinity University in San Antonio, Texas. After graduating from Indiana University with a master's degree in library science, I came back to San Antonio to work when my husband, Joe, joined the engineering staff at Kelly Air Force Base. I earned tenure as the monographs cataloger at Trinity University's Coates Library from 1990 to 1999; then I left the library to homeschool my two daughters, Valerie and Elena. My family moved to Germany in 2000, and we lived for seven years in the Rheinland Pfalz region, not far from the old Roman city of Trier. We returned to San Antonio in the summer I was born Clare Buckalew in Fort Worth, Texas, and grew up in Denton, Texas, a city north of Dallas. I earned my B.A. in Russian with a minor in Latin from Trinity University in San Antonio, Texas. After graduating from Indiana University with a master's degree in library science, I came back to San Antonio to work when my husband, Joe, joined the engineering staff at Kelly Air Force Base. I earned tenure as the monographs cataloger at Trinity University's Coates Library from 1990 to 1999; then I left the library to homeschool my two daughters, Valerie and Elena. My family moved to Germany in 2000, and we lived for seven years in the Rheinland Pfalz region, not far from the old Roman city of Trier. We returned to San Antonio in the summer of 2007, when my younger daughter Elena began college. In 2012, now grandparents, Joe and I moved back to Germany, where we are once again enjoying the bike trails, wine fests, and amazing travel opportunities. We hope to live here at least through 2017. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/8688.Eric_Flint", "name": "Eric Flint", "birthDate": "1947-02-06 00:00:00", "deathDate": "2022-07-17 00:00:00", "genres": ["Science Fiction & Fantasy"], "avgRating": 3.98, "reviewsCount": 6430, "ratingsCount": 141108, "about": "Eric Flint was a New York Times bestselling American author, editor, and e-publisher. The majority of his main works were alternate history science fiction, but he also wrote humorous fantasy adventures."}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/6879912.Jettie_Woodruff", "name": "Jettie Woodruff", "genres": ["Humor and Comedy", "Romance", "Self Help"], "avgRating": 4.0, "reviewsCount": 3969, "ratingsCount": 26749, "about": "I am a story teller, a life coach, and sometimes a little crazy. I\u2019m at an amazing time in my life where doors are opening, adventures are happening, and new friends are being made. Life is fun and I want to share that joy with the world. I\u2019m Jettie and I am unapolgetically me.\"I'm selfish, impatient, and a little insecure. I make mistakes, I'm out of control, and at times hard to handle. But if you can't handle me at my worst, then you sure as hell don't deserve me at my best.\"Marilyn Monroe I am a story teller, a life coach, and sometimes a little crazy. I\u2019m at an amazing time in my life where doors are opening, adventures are happening, and new friends are being made. Life is fun and I want to share that joy with the world. I\u2019m Jettie and I am unapolgetically me.\"I'm selfish, impatient, and a little insecure. I make mistakes, I'm out of control, and at times hard to handle. But if you can't handle me at my worst, then you sure as hell don't deserve me at my best.\"Marilyn Monroe ...more"}
