{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/14706574.Maia_Kobabe", "name": "Maia Kobabe", "genres": ["Memoir", "Comics", "Nonfiction"], "avgRating": 4.27, "reviewsCount": 9376, "ratingsCount": 64525, "about": "Maia Kobabe is a nonbinary, queer, trans author, a voracious reader, a kpop fan, and a daydreamer. You can learn an astonishing number of intimate details about em in GENDER QUEER: A MEMOIR and in eir short comics and writing published by The New Yorker, The Nib, NPR, Time Magazine, The Washington Post and in many print anthologies. GENDER QUEER won a Stonewall Honor and an Alex Award from the American Library Association in 2020. It was also the number one most challenged book in the United States in 2021, 2022, and 2023. Maia's second book is BREATHE: JOURNEYS TO HEALTHY BINDING written with Dr Sarah Peitzmeier (Dutton, 2024). E is currently working on SAACHI'S STORIES with Lucky Srikumar (Scholastic Graphix, 2026). redgoldsparks on insta Maia Kobabe is a nonbinary, queer, trans author, a voracious reader, a kpop fan, and a daydreamer. You can learn an astonishing number of intimate details about em in GENDER QUEER: A MEMOIR and in eir short comics and writing published by The New Yorker, The Nib, NPR, Time Magazine, The Washington Post and in many print anthologies. GENDER QUEER won a Stonewall Honor and an Alex Award from the American Library Association in 2020. It was also the number one most challenged book in the United States in 2021, 2022, and 2023. Maia's second book is BREATHE: JOURNEYS TO HEALTHY BINDING written with Dr Sarah Peitzmeier (Dutton, 2024). E is currently working on SAACHI'S STORIES with Lucky Srikumar (Scholastic Graphix, 2026). redgoldsparks on instagrampatreon.com/maiakobabe redgoldsparks.tumblr.com ...more"}
