{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/17153178.Moss_Whelan", "name": "Moss Whelan", "genres": ["Science Fiction", "Poetry", "Fantasy"], "influences": ["Michael Moorcock", "Frank Herbert", "J.R.R. Tolkien", "C.S. Lewis", "Michael Moor"], "avgRating": 4.32, "reviewsCount": 20, "ratingsCount": 47, "about": "Moss Whelan (1968) born in Vancouver, British Columbia, is the Canadian author of Gray Hawk of Terrapin published on January the 12th, 2018. He is an English Literature Bachelor of Arts, a Creative Writing Associate, and possesses a Diploma in Writing for Film, Television, and Interactive Media. He is active in the online Fantasy community and teaches Creative Writing. His work depicts a return to transcendent self-esteem in contrast with worldviews that shape perceived reality. He received the President\u2019s Award at Douglas College and the M. Sheila O\u2019Connel Undergraduate Prize in Children's Literature at Simon Fraser University. A survivor of PTSD, he hopes to be a voice for continued access to mental health. Moss Whelan (1968) born in Vancouver, British Columbia, is the Canadian author of Gray Hawk of Terrapin published on January the 12th, 2018. He is an English Literature Bachelor of Arts, a Creative Writing Associate, and possesses a Diploma in Writing for Film, Television, and Interactive Media. He is active in the online Fantasy community and teaches Creative Writing. His work depicts a return to transcendent self-esteem in contrast with worldviews that shape perceived reality. He received the President\u2019s Award at Douglas College and the M. Sheila O\u2019Connel Undergraduate Prize in Children's Literature at Simon Fraser University. A survivor of PTSD, he hopes to be a voice for continued access to mental health. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/670307.Friedrich_A_Hayek", "name": "Friedrich A. Hayek", "birthDate": "1899-05-08 00:00:00", "deathDate": "1992-03-23 00:00:00", "genres": ["Economics", "Politics", "Philosophy"], "influences": ["Ernst Mach", "Friedrich von Wieser", "John Locke", "Max Weber", "John ", "Carl Menger", "Adam Smith", "Bernard Mandeville", "Ludwig von Mises", "David Hume"], "avgRating": 4.17, "reviewsCount": 2404, "ratingsCount": 34507, "about": "Friedrich August von Hayek CH was an Austrian and British economist and philosopher known for his defense of classical liberalism and free-market capitalism against socialist and collectivist thought. He is considered by some to be one of the most important economists and political philosophers of the twentieth century. Hayek's account of how changing prices communicate signals which enable individuals to coordinate their plans is widely regarded as an important achievement in economics. Hayek also wrote on the topics of jurisprudence, neuroscience and the history of ideas.Hayek is one of the most influential members of the Austrian School of economics, and in 1974 shared the Nobel Memorial Prize in Economics with Gunnar Myrdal \"for their p Friedrich August von Hayek CH was an Austrian and British economist and philosopher known for his defense of classical liberalism and free-market capitalism against socialist and collectivist thought. He is considered by some to be one of the most important economists and political philosophers of the twentieth century. Hayek's account of how changing prices communicate signals which enable individuals to coordinate their plans is widely regarded as an important achievement in economics. Hayek also wrote on the topics of jurisprudence, neuroscience and the history of ideas.Hayek is one of the most influential members of the Austrian School of economics, and in 1974 shared the Nobel Memorial Prize in Economics with Gunnar Myrdal \"for their pioneering work in the