{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/17287280.Daire_Feeney", "name": "Daire Feeney", "genres": ["Memoir", "Humor and Comedy", "Nonfiction"], "avgRating": 4.39, "reviewsCount": 4, "ratingsCount": 18, "about": "Daire Freeney is the first-generation son of Irish immigrants who, after falling on hard financial times, and a subsequent failed suicide attempt, finds himself seeking employment at his old high school job as a Fifth Avenue doorman.Daire suffers from severe dyslexia and to overcome this he would tap into his passion for crossword puzzles. This practice of finding jumbled/hidden words was a method to rewire how the brain syncs with the eyes. It also helped Daire with reconciling how he views the world around him. He employed this analytical corrective method throughout all his writing and rewriting over the painstaking 10 years that it took to churn out the BOAT SHOES series. As a result, there are a lot of purposefully placed imagery (from Daire Freeney is the first-generation son of Irish immigrants who, after falling on hard financial times, and a subsequent failed suicide attempt, finds himself seeking employment at his old high school job as a Fifth Avenue doorman.Daire suffers from severe dyslexia and to overcome this he would tap into his passion for crossword puzzles. This practice of finding jumbled/hidden words was a method to rewire how the brain syncs with the eyes. It also helped Daire with reconciling how he views the world around him. He employed this analytical corrective method throughout all his writing and rewriting over the painstaking 10 years that it took to churn out the BOAT SHOES series. As a result, there are a lot of purposefully placed imagery (from the cover art to the Illuminati/freemason handshakes purposefully placed throughout the novel), to hidden words and ideas throughout both books. ...more"}
