{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/5314499.Carrie_Salo", "name": "Carrie Salo", "genres": ["Mystery & Thrillers", "History", "Horror"], "influences": ["Douglas Preston", "Lincoln Child", "Michael Crichton", "Dean Koontz", "Stephen King", "Lincoln "], "avgRating": 4.08, "reviewsCount": 42, "ratingsCount": 155, "about": "BiographyCarrie Salo is a dark storyteller and award-winning author of supernatural thrillers. Classically trained at an Ivy League university, she studied the works of master storytellers seven stories underground in the muffled heart of one of the world 's largest libraries.Carrie seeks to wield unrelenting suspense in her own exploration of all things (especially true things) that keep us awake at night. She has written under the guidance of two bestselling and national prize-winning authors. Her extensive travels have taken her to many haunted places, including the private catacombs of the Vatican. The Sounding is Carrie's debut novel.Carrie enjoys the smell of old books, New York riesling, late night jogging and thunderstorms, though n BiographyCarrie Salo is a dark storyteller and award-winning author of supernatural thrillers. Classically trained at an Ivy League university, she studied the works of master storytellers seven stories underground in the muffled heart of one of the world 's largest libraries.Carrie seeks to wield unrelenting suspense in her own exploration of all things (especially true things) that keep us awake at night. She has written under the guidance of two bestselling and national prize-winning authors. Her extensive travels have taken her to many haunted places, including the private catacombs of the Vatican. The Sounding is Carrie's debut novel.Carrie enjoys the smell of old books, New York riesling, late night jogging and thunderstorms, though not in that order. Storytelling is Carrie's secret life. While she looks into all the dark corners by night, by day she is an advertising copywriter. ...more"}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/113844.Elizabeth_Marie_Pope", "name": "Elizabeth Marie Pope", "birthDate": "1917-05-01 00:00:00", "deathDate": "1992-01-01 00:00:00", "genres": ["Young Adult", "History"], "avgRating": 4.11, "reviewsCount": 1314, "ratingsCount": 13025, "about": "Born in Washington D.C. on May 1, 1917, Pope later graduated from Bryn Mawr College and then earned her Ph. D. in English literature from John Hopkins University. Next she began teaching at Mills College in Oakland, California and remained there for many years. Beginning as an assistant professor and moving up to hold the position of professor and chairman of the department, Pope excelled as an instructor. Also an author, Pope concentrated mostly on Milton, Shakespeare, and Elizabethan England, and she traveled abroad in order to do historical research for her book The Perilous Guard which was selected for the Newbery Honor Book Award in 1975. Pope passed away in 1992."}
{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/3486206.Stephanie_Douglas", "name": "Stephanie Douglas", "genres": ["Young Adult", "Science Fiction", "Suspense"], "avgRating": 4.19, "reviewsCount": 7, "ratingsCount": 31, "about": "Stephanie Douglas is a Young Adult author who loves to dabble in the dissident and vulnerable world of dystopian adventure. As a young girl, Stephanie poured through books and ultimately fell in love with stories where characters were forced to rely on their wit and courage to carry them through danger, hardship, and loss \u2013 who at the end of the story, were irreversibly transformed into the leader they were destined to be. With a love for storytelling and an equal passion for music, Stephanie is currently working on books two and three in the Callasandra series, which, like Callasandra Fractured, will be filled with twists and turns and incredible music. Stay tuned!"}
