{"url": "https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/59713.Jon_McGregor", "name": "Jon McGregor", "influences": ["Char", "Alice Munro", "Charles Simic", "Douglas Coupland", "Raymond Carver", "Richard Brautigan"], "avgRating": 3.7, "reviewsCount": 4741, "ratingsCount": 34299, "about": "Jon McGregor is a British author who has written three novels. His first novel, If Nobody Speaks of Remarkable Things, was nominated for the 2002 Booker Prize and was the winner of both the Betty Trask Prize and the Somerset Maugham Award in 2003. So Many Ways to Begin was published in 2006 and was on the Booker prize long list. Even the Dogs was published in 2010, and his newest work, Reservoir 13, was published in April 2017."}
